Package: keel-web
Architecture: all
Depends:
 anubis (>= 1.27.0-0+keel3),
 keel (>= 0.15.0),
 keel-core,
 keel-overlay-anubis,
 keel-overlay-coraza (>= 0.1.2),
 keel-overlay-nginx,
 ${misc:Depends},
Description: Keel Web, the base of every Keel web appliance
 The appliance manifest of Keel Web (handbook decisions 0030 and 0041),
 installed as /usr/share/keel/appliances/web.yaml: Keel Core plus the
 nginx, coraza and anubis overlays, Nginx alone in a simple installation
 and the three of them in the cloud modes.
 .
 It also ships the Anubis front of the default site,
 /etc/nginx/sites-available/default-anubis (HTTPS with the machine's
 certificate, port 80 redirecting to it), and the state hook that keel
 spec apply runs when the anubis overlay is turned on or off, which puts
 that front in place of Debian's default site and back. Installing it
 enables nothing.
